---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LegalShell from '../components/legal/LegalShell.astro';
import { legalPage } from '../data/legal';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

const page = legalPage(
  'terms',
  '/terms/',
  'Terms of Service | Tip Top Hybrid',
  'The terms that apply when you use the Tip Top Hybrid website, request an estimate, or have us repair or service your vehicle.',
);
---

<BaseLayout page={page}>
  <LegalShell title="Terms of Service" updated="November 15, 2026">
    <p>
      These Terms of Service (“Terms”) govern your use of <strong>www.tiptophybrid.com</strong> (the
      “Site”) and any estimate, appointment or repair service you request from
      <strong>Tip Top Hybrid</strong> (“we”, “us”, “our”). By using the Site or booking service, you
      accept these Terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the Site.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      Tip Top Hybrid is an independent hybrid vehicle repair shop located at
      {SITE.street}, Upland, CA 91786. You can reach us on {SITE.phone} or at
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Website content</h2>
    <p>
      The content on this Site — including service descriptions, pricing guidance, articles and
      frequently asked questions — is provided for general information only. It is not a diagnosis,
      a repair order or a guarantee that a particular repair will fix a particular symptom. Hybrid
      systems vary by model, year and condition, and only an in-person inspection can confirm what
      your vehicle needs.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Estimates and pricing</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Estimates given online, by phone or in person are good-faith estimates based on the information available at the time. They are not fixed-price quotes unless we state so in writing.</li>
      <li>Diagnostic time, teardown and inspection may be charged and will be explained before work begins where practicable.</li>
      <li>Additional faults, parts availability or hidden damage may change the scope and cost. We will contact you for approval before performing work that materially exceeds the approved estimate.</li>
      <li>Prices are in US dollars and may change without notice. Taxes, fees and disposal charges are additional where applicable.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Appointments, drop-off and storage</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Appointment times are targets, not guarantees. Repair duration depends on diagnosis, parts and conditions outside our control.</li>
      <li>You authorise us to operate, road-test and move your vehicle for the purpose of inspection, diagnosis, repair and quality checks.</li>
      <li>Please remove valuables and personal items before drop-off. We are not responsible for items left in the vehicle.</li>
      <li>Vehicles must be collected within a reasonable time after we notify you that work is complete. Storage and lien rights for uncollected vehicles are governed by applicable California law.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Parts and warranty</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We may use new, remanufactured or reconditioned parts depending on the repair and your approval. The parts used are recorded on your invoice.</li>
      <li>Our workmanship and any parts warranty we provide are stated on your invoice or estimate. Manufacturer and supplier warranties pass through to you where applicable.</li>
      <li>Warranty coverage does not apply to unrelated failures, misuse, accidents, modifications, or work performed by another shop after our repair.</li>
      <li>Except as expressly stated on your invoice, and to the fullest extent permitted by law, we disclaim all other warranties, including implied warranties of merchantability and fitness for a particular purpose.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. Your responsibilities</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Give us accurate contact, vehicle and service information, and tell us about previous repairs, modifications or known faults.</li>
      <li>Ensure the vehicle is delivered with the keys, wheel-lock key and any security codes we need.</li>
      <li>Pay the invoiced amount when the work is complete, unless we have agreed other terms in writing.</li>
      <li>Use this Site lawfully and do not attempt to interfere with it, scrape it, or submit false or abusive enquiries.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      The Site’s text, layout, logos, photographs and other content are owned by us or used with
      permission and are protected by copyright and trademark law. You may view and print pages for
      your own non-commercial use; any other reproduction or commercial use requires our written
      permission.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Third-party links</h2>
    <p>
      The Site may link to third-party websites, including Google Maps and social media. We do not
      control those sites and are not responsible for their content or practices.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, we are not liable for indirect, incidental, special or
      consequential damages arising from your use of the Site or from services, including lost
      profits, lost time or loss of use of a vehicle. Nothing in these Terms limits liability that
      cannot lawfully be limited, including liability for our own negligence where such a limitation
      is prohibited. The Site is provided “as is” and we do not warrant that it will be uninterrupted
      or error-free.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Indemnity</h2>
    <p>
      You agree to indemnify us against claims, losses or costs arising from your breach of these
      Terms, your misuse of the Site, or inaccurate information you provide to us.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of California. Any dispute that cannot be
      resolved informally will be brought in the state or federal courts located in San Bernardino
      County, California, unless applicable law requires otherwise.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these Terms from time to time. The revision date above shows the current version,
      which applies from the date it is posted. Your continued use of the Site after a change means
      you accept the updated Terms.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these Terms? Call {SITE.phone}, email
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>, or write to us at {SITE.street}, Upland, CA
      91786.
    </p>
  </LegalShell>
</BaseLayout>
